DIFF(1)

NAME
     diff - show the lines that differ between two files

SYNOPSIS
     diff file1 file2

DESCRIPTION
     Compares two files line by line and prints only what differs.

         < line      is in file1 only
         > line      is in file2 only

     The lines of numbers and letters in between say where: 3d2 means
     line 3 of file1 has no partner in file2; 7a8 means line 8 of file2
     was added after line 7 of file1; c means the lines changed.

     If the files are the same, diff prints nothing.

EXAMPLES
     diff /tmp/billed /tmp/used

SEE ALSO
     sort(1)
